`authors.routes.ts` handles HTTP only:

```ts
app.post('/', { schema: { tags: ['authors'], body: CreateAuthorBody,
    response: { 201: Type.Object({ data: Author }), 400: ErrorBody, 401: ErrorBody } } },
  async (req, reply) => reply.code(201).send({ data: await createAuthor(db, req.body) }));

app.get('/:authorId', { schema: { params: AuthorParams,
    response: { 200: Type.Object({ data: Author }), 400: ErrorBody, 401: ErrorBody, 404: ErrorBody } } },
  async (req) => ({ data: await getAuthor(db, req.params.authorId) }));
```

`domain/author-name.ts`: plain TypeScript, no framework imports.

```ts
export function parseAuthorName(raw: string): string {
  const name = raw.trim();
  if (name.length === 0) throw new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', [{ field: 'name', code: 'REQUIRED' }]);
  return name;
}
```

`application/create-author.ts`:

```ts
export async function createAuthor(db: Db, input: { name: string }) {
  const [row] = await db.insert(authors).values({ name: parseAuthorName(input.name) }).returning();
  return toAuthor(row!);   // maps explicitly: id, name, createdAt.toISOString()
}
```

`application/get-author.ts` returns the row from `select … where id = $1` or throws `AppError('RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND')`.

The ORM row is never returned directly. The response schema also drops any unlisted column.

### Integration test sketch (`authors.int.test.ts`)

```ts
const auth = { authorization: 'Bearer test-secret' };
it('creates an author and persists it', async () => {
  const res = await app.inject({ method: 'POST', url: '/api/v1/authors', headers: auth, payload: { name: 'Ursula K. Le Guin' } });
  expect(res.statusCode).toBe(201);
  const { data } = res.json();
  expect(data).toMatchObject({ name: 'Ursula K. Le Guin' });
  const rows = await db.select().from(authors).where(eq(authors.id, data.id));
  expect(rows).toHaveLength(1);
});
it('rejects unknown fields', async () => {
  const res = await app.inject({ method: 'POST', url: '/api/v1/authors', headers: auth, payload: { name: 'X', role: 'admin' } });
  expect(res.statusCode).toBe(400);
  expect(res.json().error).toMatchObject({ code: 'VALIDATION_ERROR', details: [{ field: 'role', code: 'UNKNOWN_FIELD' }] });
});
```

`test/global-setup.ts` starts `@testcontainers/postgresql` on `postgres:18`, applies `migrations/`, and exposes `DATABASE_URL`. Tests never depend on the compose stack.

